playing clinical signs of severe growth faltering. Establish mandatory 7-day feeding logs under Posyandu health worker supervision.\n\n### Directive 3: Mass Maternal Anemia & Prevention Rollout (Days 8\u201311)\n* **Action:** Mobilize healthcare workers in High and Moderate districts (Labuhan, Deli, Denai, Tembung) to conduct targeted distribution of **Iron Folate packs** to pregnant and lactating mothers exhibiting signs of anemia.\n* **Target:** Distribute **1,228 Iron Folate packs** across Labuhan, Deli, Denai, and Tembung alongside **1,268 Fortified PMT boxes** for toddlers showing early growth decelerations.\n\n### Directive 4: Integrated WASH Triage & Telemetry Reporting (Days 12\u201314)\n* **Action:** Partner with local sanitation officers in districts where `poor_sanitation_pct` exceeds 0.40 to deploy temporary point-of-use water purification tablets alongside PMT distribution.\n* **Target:** Mandate bi-weekly Posyandu telemetry uploads to the CRESCA engine to track individual child growth trajectories against the 90-day Poisson forecast models. Any non-responsive cases must be escalated immediately to secondary referral facilities.\n\n---\n\n**AUTHORIZATION SIGN-OFF:**  \n*CRESCA AI \u2014 Precision Nutrition Logistics Engine*  \n*Document Ref: CNP-90D-OPT-2023-V1*  \n*Status: APPROVED FOR IMMEDIATE FIELD EXECUTION*",
